From 3474287c931904029fe5f612ab872690c11cfdc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:06:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/22] thingino-raptor: raptor-watchdog fault reports and
 recovery

raptor-watchdog and S34raptor-watchdog, installed on SigmaStar builds. Every
5 s: a new [MI ERR] line saves a gzipped fault report (the newest 5 are
kept); a stalled encoder port, or rvd stuck in the driver, gets a report and
a raptor restart, then a reboot, at most 3 an hour. The Infinity6C encoder
can wedge while the camera stays up, and the kernel ring that holds the cause
wraps within minutes. rvd gone for 15 s while rsd still runs (the kernel
killed it for memory, on a 64 MB board) also gets a report and a restart. A
quiet poll starts two processes, the sleep and one awk.

For the same boards the agent listener answers at most 3 requests at once
(AGENT_MAX_REQUESTS), and it and what it starts go before the video daemons
when memory runs out.
---
 package/thingino-agent/files/S95agent         |   4 +
 package/thingino-agent/files/agentd-native.c  |  28 +-
 .../thingino-raptor/files/S34raptor-watchdog  |  39 +++
 package/thingino-raptor/files/raptor-watchdog | 310 ++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 379 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100755 package/thingino-raptor/files/S34raptor-watchdog
 create mode 100755 package/thingino-raptor/files/raptor-watchdog

